From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:45:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] ASoC: samsung: abox: require a bound ABOX GIC before
 probing

The probe registers its IPC handlers through the ABOX GIC driver's data,
but only checked that the GIC platform device existed, not that its
driver had bound; link order alone kept the data valid (a NULL GIC
driver data panics in abox_gic_register_irq_handler(), seen in a test
build in M10.2 A1d). The lookup also ran after the IOMMU mappings, so a
deferral there would leave mappings that make the next probe fail.

Look the GIC up first, before anything is allocated or mapped, defer
until its driver is bound, and add a device link so the GIC cannot
unbind while the ABOX uses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ib04ba5accb09c5d39da151823632a42fdd9aa13e
---
 sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
index f216c3d60..a00809ff8 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -5896,10 +5896,32 @@ static int samsung_abox_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct platform_device *pdev_tmp;
 	struct abox_data *data;
 	phys_addr_t paddr __maybe_unused;
+	struct device *dev_gic;
 	int ret, i;
 
 	dev_info(dev, "%s\n", __func__);
 
+	/*
+	 * The ABOX GIC driver must be bound first: its driver data is used
+	 * below to register the IPC handlers. Check before anything is
+	 * allocated or mapped so a deferral leaves no state behind, and link
+	 * the devices so the GIC cannot go away under the ABOX.
+	 */
+	np_tmp = of_parse_phandle(np, "abox_gic", 0);
+	if (!np_tmp)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "no abox_gic phandle\n");
+	pdev_tmp = of_find_device_by_node(np_tmp);
+	of_node_put(np_tmp);
+	if (!pdev_tmp)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER, "abox_gic not created\n");
+	dev_gic = &pdev_tmp->dev;
+	if (!dev_get_drvdata(dev_gic) ||
+	    !device_link_add(dev, dev_gic, DL_FLAG_AUTOREMOVE_CONSUMER)) {
+		put_device(dev_gic);
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER, "abox_gic not bound\n");
+	}
+	put_device(dev_gic);
+
 	data = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*data), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -6136,17 +6158,7 @@ static int samsung_abox_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
-	np_tmp = of_parse_phandle(np, "abox_gic", 0);
-	if (!np_tmp) {
-		dev_err(dev, "Failed to get abox_gic device node\n");
-		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
-	}
-	pdev_tmp = of_find_device_by_node(np_tmp);
-	if (!pdev_tmp) {
-		dev_err(dev, "Failed to get abox_gic platform device\n");
-		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
-	}
-	data->dev_gic = &pdev_tmp->dev;
+	data->dev_gic = dev_gic;
 
 	if (abox_test_quirk(data, ABOX_QUIRK_SHARE_VTS_SRAM)) {
 		np_tmp = of_parse_phandle(np, "vts", 0);
